i'll never forget the first time i saw  harry potter and the sorcerer's stone at  least the book cover i was in the  seventh grade and flipping through one  of those little scholastic book order  forms which they still send out today by  the way and it was really mary grand  praise cover of harry potter and the  sorcerer's stone that just immediately  drew my attention from there i read the  description and almost was instantly  hooked i knew it was a book that i just  had to read now i was a decent reader as  a kid but wouldn't say it's something i  love to do that is until harry potter  and reading harry potter really changed  everything for me long before there were  movies games theme parks i and numerous  others from my generation had already  started to imagine what hogwarts would  be like in our head what would it be  like to be sorted into a house with  others who shared a common goal and  interest and then of course to learn  about a whole new fantastical world of  magic it was really this sense of wonder  and excitement from so many kids in that  time that led to midnight launch parties  fan websites podcasts movies a theme  park and of course video games well  turns out a lot of those kids me you're  a wizard kids my age are now adults and  for more than 20 years we've been  waiting for a video game we've been  imagining a video game that would let us  step into this wonderful world not as  hairy but as our own witch or wizard you  see just recently the first official  hogwarts legacy trailer actually  eclipsed 29 million views on  playstation's youtube channel which make  it the most viewed video focusing on a  single game on their entire channel and  the third most viewed video across their  entire channel of any kind and when you  consider they have characters like  kratos nathan drake and even spider-man  how is it that a game set in the  wizarding world not even dedicated to  harry potter himself how is it that a  game like that has become one of the  most anticipated one of the most hyped  games in recent memory i think it's  simple it's shaping up to be a game that  fans have been dreaming of for more than  20 years now it's true there have been  numerous potter games over the years but  the majority have been third person  action with puzzle elements that follow  harry's story harry potter and the  philosopher's stone on pc or the  original playstation is the game many  fans think of when they remember back to  the origins of those first harry potter  video games the pc version put players  in control of harry after his arrival at  hogwarts some of the spells in the game  were flpendo alohomora guardium leviosa  lumos and incendio the spells were  contextual and while they could be cast  at any time by the player they would  only react to specific objects in the  world the pc version actually sold  really well over a million copies and  the playstation version saw ridiculous  sales numbers more than eight million  copies sold and it's actually the sixth  best selling playstation title of all  time and when you think how big of a  seller the playstation was and all the  great games that were on that system  that is a huge accomplishment top six  all time on playstation it's kind of  interesting that playstation seems to  have a marketing deal for hogwarts  legacy given that harry potter really  had some of its early beginnings right  there on the playstation now in the  years that would follow numerous other  potter games were released with varying  levels of success some are remembered  fondly others just outright bad but none  have even really attempted or even come  close to have attempted what hogwarts  legacy is trying to do now while  hogwarts legacy will keep the third  person perspective and likely some of  the action and puzzle elements from  those earlier games it's being developed  as a completely open world action rpg  and of course instead of following  harry's story this will be the story of  our own witch or wizard set in 1890 long  before harry's arrival at hogwarts even  before dumbledore's arrival at hogwarts  according to the official hogwarts  legacy website the story has players  experiencing life as a student at  hogwarts school of witchcraft and  wizardry like never before as they live  the unwritten and embark on a dangerous  journey to uncover a hidden truth of the  wizarding world so you see there we got  that fresh new mystery you know it  wouldn't be a harry potter story without  a good mystery to solve but what about  the canon and the lore that we already  know well the site also says this while  portkey games are not direct adaptations  of the books and films the games are  firmly rooted in the magical universe of  the wizarding world now this  appreciation of the source material and  the focus on so many of the things that  fans have wanted for many years the  ability to make our own adventure or as  they say live the unwritten is one of  the main reasons i think that fans are  so hyped for the project even with the  limited information we have about how  the game will actually play and even  though admittedly it's avalanche's first  attempt at an action rpg they're not a  developer that's known for this and at  this stage we truly don't know how the  game will pan out i'll be honest with  you guys we just don't know but there is  one thing that was completely clear from  the developer interviews that were shown  after the gameplay reveal trailer back  in march that i don't think anyone can  dispute and that is that avalanche as a  team they truly care about this project  that they're working on they are  passionate about it they are fans of  this world and they really want to  deliver on that promise of a wizarding  world game that ultimately captures all  that magic and lives up to the hype that  truly has been building for more than 20  years now the movies the books they've  all touched me in such a way like it  makes me want to go to  experience hogwarts makes me put in so  much more detail into this game this is  the game that they've dreamed of for 20  years  [Music]  hogwarts legacy is undoubtedly the most  bold attempt yet at creating a wizarding  world game fans can get lost in it's a  game where fans are just hoping they can  wander the halls of hogwarts for hours  on end discovering new areas discovering  new secrets hidden passages overhearing  conversations and then starting new  quests as a result of those  conversations being the witch or wizard  we want to be it truly seems like they  are shooting for the moon i mean that  fully explorable hogwarts an elaborate  spell casting system we're going to have  upgrades we're going to be able to  unlock new abilities we're going to be  able to customize the look of our  character we can visit hogsmeade we can  visit the grounds even and meet people  along the outside of hogwarts not to  mention an entirely new mystery that who  knows may even involve merlin now as i  mentioned in the beginning i still  remember all those years ago when i  first opened the pages of harry potter  and the sorcerer's stone and no doubt i  think i and many other fans who have  grown up with this series are going to  have similar memories playing hogwarts  legacy for the first time when we first  hold that game in our hands or if you're  a digital only when you first boot it up  on your system it's going to be an  incredibly memorable moment that has  been building for a long time and here's  to hoping hogwarts legacy can deliver on  what is undoubtedly a very lofty promise  it's going to be a challenge there is no  doubt that this is a tall tall order but  who knows perhaps this could just kick  off a new era for wizarding world video  games now if you'd like an extended look  at the history of all the harry potter  video games so far their charm and all  their flaws check out the video on the  right side of your screen now as always  thank you all so much for watching i'll  talk to you again soon
 

